Here I go

If a spellbook is too faint to read anymore it changes into a spellbook 
of blank paper.  So the spellbook is actually gone.  "Recovery" like a 
unrusting a rusty sword is impossible because the actual object is 
different.  So yes, a magic marker is the way to go.

The best way to get a magic marker is to get a large pile of useless 
tools (extra whistles, extra leashes, chests, large boxes, lamps that 
have burned out), and polymorph them.

Whenever I play a game I always build a large cache of blank scrolls.  I 
usually get them from dipping useless or dangerous scrolls into a 
fountain.  The hardest part is trying to find enough magic markers to 
write on them.  

I also build up large caches of water by dipping useless potions into a 
fountain (twice), and then converting a while bunch with one dipping.  
Blessed potions and scrolls are the best way to make the best of them.  

